videocodec.library examples
===========================

Two small programs, written to be copied: each uses nothing but
videocodec.library's headers and Picasso96's.

VCPlay - a video player
-----------------------

Plays an H.264 or H.265 elementary stream (a .h264 file, or a .h265, .hevc
or .265 one) in a window on the Workbench. One decoder session does the work:
the hardware decodes, the VideoCore scales and converts each picture to the
screen's pixel format, and VCPlay copies it into the window with
p96WritePixelArray() when it is due. It shows the sessions: packets in,
frames out, VC_Poll() and a signal. H.265 needs rpivid.codec; its pictures
reach the screen's format through a converter videocodec.library puts
behind the decoder, which VC_QueryCodec() lists in ChainOutputFormats.

    VCPlay video.h264
    VCPlay video.h265

The close gadget, Ctrl-C or the end of the stream stops it.

VCShow - a picture viewer
-------------------------

Shows a JPEG, PNG, GIF, BMP or PPM picture in a window on the Workbench.
VC_GetImageInfo() reads the picture's size from its header; one
VC_DecodeImageTags() call has the VideoCore decode it, scale it to the window
and convert it to the screen's pixel format. It shows the image calls, and
where a viewer falls back to its own decoder: what the hardware would get
wrong (a progressive JPEG, a 16-bit PNG, ...) is refused before the hardware
sees it.

    VCShow photo.jpg

The close gadget or Ctrl-C closes it.

Files
-----

    VCPlay.c, VCShow.c    the sources
    VCPlay, VCShow        built from them

Building
--------

With the m68k-amigaos-gcc toolchain (bebbo's amiga-gcc), in this drawer:

    m68k-amigaos-gcc -Os -mcrt=nix20 -I../../include VCPlay.c -o VCPlay
    m68k-amigaos-gcc -Os -mcrt=nix20 -I../../include VCShow.c -o VCShow

../../include is the archive's Developer/include drawer, which holds
videocodec.library's headers. The Picasso96 headers come from P96Develop
(Aminet); the toolchain image the driver stack is built with has them.

More
----

The API's contract is the opening comment of
Developer/include/libraries/videocodec.h. The developer guide
(developer-guide.md) is in the source repository:
https://github.com/rondoval/emu68-vchiq-library
